course: dictionary
lesson: 861
title: Muscles that work in pairs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Your biceps is a muscle. It is the big muscle at the front of your upper arm, and when it gets shorter it pulls your forearm up, which bends your elbow. «Bend your arm and feel the biceps at the front go hard as it pulls the forearm up.»
explain: A muscle can only pull, never push. So to straighten your arm again, a different muscle has to pull the other way: the triceps at the back. «The biceps bends the arm and the triceps straightens it.» The two muscles work in pairs.
explain: Biceps can also name a similar muscle at the back of the thigh, which is the top part of your leg. The word is the same, so look at the sentence to see which body part it means.
fact: The biceps is the big muscle at the front of your upper arm that bends your elbow.
fact: Biceps can also name a similar muscle at the back of the thigh.
fact: Muscles can only pull, never push.
fact: The triceps, at the back of the arm, pulls to straighten the elbow.
fact: Biceps is a noun, and its plural is also biceps.
exercise: «Bend your arm and feel the biceps at the front go hard.» Which muscle is the biceps? | The bone in your forearm | The muscle at the back of your upper arm | The muscle at the front of your shin | *The big muscle at the front of your upper arm
exercise: «Muscles can only pull, never push.» Which muscle straightens the arm? | The biceps | The elbow joint | *The triceps | The forearm bone
exercise: Find and copy the word that names the muscle that straightens the arm. | forearm | *triceps | bends | biceps
test: What does the biceps do when it gets shorter? | Straightens the elbow | Makes the arm longer | Pushes the bones apart | *Bends the elbow
test: Why do muscles work in pairs? | *Because a muscle can only pull, so a second muscle must pull the other way to undo the movement | Because the biceps is always bigger than the triceps | Because muscles can push and pull at the same time | Because bones cannot move without help from the skin
exam: Where is the biceps found in the first meaning of the word? | The back of the upper arm | The shin | The front of the thigh | *The front of the upper arm
